## Authority file responsibilities

| File | Purpose | Should own data? | Should call |
|---|---|---:|---|
| `authorityRegistryArchitecture.ts` | Defines authority registry types, ranking, metadata, safety structure | Yes, types only | Nothing heavy |
| `verifiedAuthoritySeedRegistry.ts` | Seed verified authority entries | Yes, seed data | Registry architecture |
| `authorityRetrievalEngine.ts` | Searches/ranks verified authority entries | No permanent state | Seed registry |
| `authorityDisplayEngine.ts` | Converts authorities into display groups/cards | No | Retrieval engine |
| `authorityNavigator.ts` | Normalizes request context, routes authority needs, builds hooks | No | Retrieval/display through adapters |
| `authorityIntegrationHub.ts` | Single consumer-facing entry point | No | Navigator |
| `authorityWorkflowBridge.ts` | Converts workflow blockers/readiness into authority needs | No | Integration hub |
| `authorityBrainBridge.ts` | Converts Brain output into authority signals | No | Integration hub |
| `authorityCaseSystemBridge.ts` | Converts MasterCaseSchema / CaseSystemAssembly into authority signals | No | Brain bridge, workflow bridge, integration hub |

## Architectural judgment

This many files is acceptable **if** each layer keeps its role.

The risk is not “too many files.”  
The risk is allowing pages or older engines to bypass the bridges and directly use legal authority.

